Error [E0109]: `!` needs Bool; use `bit_not` to flip integer bits
  --> bit_not_wrong_type.jet:3:11
    |
  3 |     print(!label)
    |           ^^^^^^
 Why: Marks express ownership and outcomes; arithmetic uses named methods (D-SIGIL-ALGEBRA1=B)
 Fix: Write `value.bit_not()` for an integer, or compare the value to produce Bool
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0109
